diff --git a/third_party/bevy_shader/BENILLA.md b/third_party/bevy_shader/BENILLA.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..73004912
--- /dev/null
+++ b/third_party/bevy_shader/BENILLA.md
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# benilla's `bevy_shader` fork: what differs from upstream, and how to check
+
+Upstream: [`bevyengine/bevy`](https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy) `crates/bevy_shader`, MIT OR
+Apache-2.0, version `0.18.1`, the version the workspace lock resolves to. Wired in through
+`[patch.crates-io]` in the workspace root, the way `kira` is. The crate is copied from the cargo
+registry as published (`src/`, `Cargo.toml`, the two licence files); only `src/shader_cache.rs`
+differs.
+
+## Why a fork exists at all
+
+In the browser every pipeline is built inline. `bevy_render`'s `create_pipeline_task` has no task
+pool on wasm32 and runs each build to completion inside `PipelineCache::process_queue`, so every
+pipeline queued in a frame is built in that frame. A build is mostly the shader module: naga_oil
+composes it, naga validates it and writes WGSL, and the page hands that to WebGPU. That costs
+~125-350 ms a module on the main thread, so a frame that queued many pipelines was one long task:
+20261026a, Dalaran, `frame (login): 27 pipelines queued` at 9.4 s, and a 9.2 s covered frame at
+world entry. The page cannot draw, read a socket or land a fetch for that long.
+
+## The change: a module build gate (`src/shader_cache.rs`)
+
+`set_module_build_gate(fn() -> bool)` installs, once per process, a function `ShaderCache::get` asks
+before it composes and creates a module it has not built yet. When the gate answers `false`, `get`
+returns `PipelineCacheError::ShaderImportNotYetAvailable`, an error `PipelineCache::process_pipeline`
+already treats as "retry": the pipeline goes back to `Queued` and is tried again on a later frame,
+exactly like a pipeline whose shader import has not loaded yet. A module already built is never
+gated, so a pipeline whose modules exist is created at once.
+
+Without a gate installed (natively, and in every test) the crate behaves exactly as upstream.
+
+The gate itself is `benilla-app`'s `pipe_warm::build_gate`: in the browser it lets one module
+build start every frame, and more only while that frame's builds have taken less than its budget.
+To the rest of the client a deferred pipeline looks like a pipeline still compiling, the state
+every native build that is not macOS already sees (`PipeWatch::compiling`).
+
+## How to check
+
+- `diff -r ~/.cargo/registry/src/*/bevy_shader-0.18.1/src third_party/bevy_shader/src` shows the
+  gate and nothing else.
+- `benilla-app`'s `pipe_warm` tests cover the gate's frame budget.
+- Live: `__wenilla_loadtrace` frame labels carry `N shader builds deferred`, and no frame holds more
+  than one slow module build.
+
+## Dropping the fork
+
+When the workspace moves to a bevy whose pipeline cache builds asynchronously on wasm (or exposes a
+per-frame budget), delete this directory and its `[patch.crates-io]` line; `pipe_warm`'s
+`install_build_gate` is then the only caller to remove.
